Z||000002||87GTZ34||11-01-2001||10:48 AM||||Fieroman,  My experience with fuel problems is that they usually get worse with RPM (more fule needed, same fuel available).  The only exception to the rule is leaky injectors because they run rich at lower rpm and lean out as more air is added.  I'm not saying you don't have a fuel problem but it is curious that the problem is in a narrow range.<BR>How many miles on your engine, on your tuneup, has it been sitting?  For troubleshooting, I would start with the basics, vacuum leaks, ignition check etc.||||reg||1
